          {
            "number": 17,
            "text": "A heart settled upon a thoughtful understanding is as an ornament of plaster on a polished wall."
          },
          {
            "number": 18,
            "text": "Fences set on a high place will not stand against the wind; so a fearful heart in the imagination of a fool will not stand against any fear."
          },
          {
            "number": 19,
            "text": "He who pricks the eye will make tears fall. He who pricks the heart makes it show feeling."
          },
          {
            "number": 20,
            "text": "Whoever casts a stone at birds scares them away. He who insults a friend will dissolve friendship."
          },
          {
            "number": 21,
            "text": "If you have drawn a sword against a friend, don’t despair, for there may be a way back."
          },
          {
            "number": 22,
            "text": "If you have opened your mouth against a friend, don’t be afraid, for there may be reconciliation, unless it is for insulting, arrogance, disclosing of a secret, or a treacherous blow— for these things any friend will flee."
          },
          {
            "number": 23,
            "text": "Gain trust with your neighbor in his poverty, that in his prosperity you may have gladness. Stay steadfast to him in the time of his affliction, that you may be heir with him in his inheritance."
          },
          {
            "number": 24,
            "text": "Before fire is the vapor and smoke of a furnace, so insults precede bloodshed."
          },
          {
            "number": 25,
            "text": "I won’t be ashamed to shelter a friend. I won’t hide myself from his face."
          },
          {
            "number": 26,
            "text": "If any evil happens to me because of him, everyone who hears it will beware of him."
          },
          {
            "number": 27,
            "text": "Who will set a watch over my mouth, and a seal of shrewdness upon my lips, that I may not fall from it, and that my tongue may not destroy me?"
          }
